  "units": [
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-left-my-charger-p1",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-left-my-charger-p1",
      "textEn": "On Saturday I had a simple plan. I would spend the afternoon at the small library near my apartment, then meet my friend Tara for dinner.",
      "spans": [],
      "parentId": "reading-left-my-charger"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-left-my-charger-p2",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-left-my-charger-p2",
      "textEn": "I packed my laptop, a notebook, and a bottle of water. The charger was on the kitchen table, but I did not put it in my bag. I only thought about it later.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 59,
          "end": 66,
          "surface": "charger",
          "cardId": "rd5-charger",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        },
        {
          "start": 149,
          "end": 154,
          "surface": "later",
          "cardId": "l12-w-later",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-left-my-charger"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-left-my-charger-p3",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-left-my-charger-p3",
      "textEn": "The library was quiet, and I found a table by the window. For about two hours, I worked on a short presentation for a weekend class. My phone stayed in my bag.",
      "spans": [],
      "parentId": "reading-left-my-charger"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-left-my-charger-p4",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-left-my-charger-p4",
      "textEn": "Then my laptop made a soft sound. The battery was low. I looked in every pocket of my bag, and then I remembered: I had left my charger at home.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 120,
          "end": 135,
          "surface": "left my charger",
          "cardId": "rd5-left-behind",
          "form": "variant",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-left-my-charger"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-left-my-charger-p5",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-left-my-charger-p5",
      "textEn": "I did not want to lose the table. I asked the woman next to me if she could watch my notebook for ten minutes, and she said yes.",
      "spans": [],
      "parentId": "reading-left-my-charger"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-left-my-charger-p6",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-left-my-charger-p6",
      "textEn": "I walked home quickly. The charger was still on the table, next to a pile of mail. I grabbed it, locked the door, and walked back.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 27,
          "end": 34,
          "surface": "charger",
          "cardId": "rd5-charger",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        },
        {
          "start": 108,
          "end": 112,
          "surface": "door",
          "cardId": "l13-w-door",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-left-my-charger"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-left-my-charger-p7",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-left-my-charger-p7",
      "textEn": "My things were still there. I thanked the woman, plugged in the laptop, and sat down again. The rest of the afternoon went more slowly, but I finished what I needed.",
      "spans": [],
      "parentId": "reading-left-my-charger"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-left-my-charger-p8",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-left-my-charger-p8",
      "textEn": "At six, I packed up and met Tara at a noodle place down the street. I was only a little late, but I still felt rushed.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 88,
          "end": 92,
          "surface": "late",
          "cardId": "L05-V03",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-left-my-charger"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-left-my-charger-p9",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-left-my-charger-p9",
      "textEn": "I told her the story over dinner. She laughed and said she had done the same thing last month, with her camera, not her laptop.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 83,
          "end": 93,
          "surface": "last month",
          "cardId": "L08-V02",
          "form": "variant",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-left-my-charger"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-left-my-charger-p10",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-left-my-charger-p10",
      "textEn": "Next time, I will put the charger in my bag the night before, or look at the table once more before I leave. It was a small mistake, but I was glad I went back instead of giving up on the afternoon.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 26,
          "end": 33,
          "surface": "charger",
          "cardId": "rd5-charger",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        },
        {
          "start": 102,
          "end": 107,
          "surface": "leave",
          "cardId": "l14-w-leave",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        },
        {
          "start": 160,
          "end": 167,
          "surface": "instead",
          "cardId": "reading-delivery-w07",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-left-my-charger"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p1",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p1",
      "textEn": "On Tuesday morning, I was waiting for a box. I had bought a small lamp online for my sister's birthday, and the shop said it would arrive that day. I wanted it to get here in time, because I was seeing her on Friday.",
      "spans": [],
      "parentId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p2",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p2",
      "textEn": "I could not stay home and wait. I had already planned to go to the street market for fruit and bread, and my roommate was away that week. For a moment I thought about staying in, but I didn't want to waste the morning.",
      "spans": [],
      "parentId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p3",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p3",
      "textEn": "The market took longer than I thought. When I came home around noon, there was nothing at my door and no message about a locker. I stood there with my bags, feeling uneasy. I thought I had missed the courier.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 93,
          "end": 97,
          "surface": "door",
          "cardId": "l13-w-door",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        },
        {
          "start": 105,
          "end": 112,
          "surface": "message",
          "cardId": "l12-w-message",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        },
        {
          "start": 121,
          "end": 127,
          "surface": "locker",
          "cardId": "sc11-locker",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        },
        {
          "start": 189,
          "end": 195,
          "surface": "missed",
          "cardId": "l17-w-miss",
          "form": "variant",
          "priority": "primary"
        },
        {
          "start": 200,
          "end": 207,
          "surface": "courier",
          "cardId": "sc11-courier",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p4",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p4",
      "textEn": "I checked the stairs and the mailbox, then walked back up and looked again. Still nothing. I even walked to the locker by the gate, but it was empty, and my phone had no new messages.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 112,
          "end": 118,
          "surface": "locker",
          "cardId": "sc11-locker",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p5",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p5",
      "textEn": "Then I saw a piece of paper under my door. It was a short note from a neighbor I usually only smiled at in the hallway. Her name was Mrs. Tan, in 4A.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 37,
          "end": 41,
          "surface": "door",
          "cardId": "l13-w-door",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        },
        {
          "start": 70,
          "end": 78,
          "surface": "neighbor",
          "cardId": "reading-delivery-w04",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        },
        {
          "start": 111,
          "end": 118,
          "surface": "hallway",
          "cardId": "reading-delivery-w09",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p6",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p6",
      "textEn": "The note said the courier had come at ten, and she had taken the box so it would not sit in the hallway all morning. She said I could come over any time after lunch.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 18,
          "end": 25,
          "surface": "courier",
          "cardId": "sc11-courier",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        },
        {
          "start": 96,
          "end": 103,
          "surface": "hallway",
          "cardId": "reading-delivery-w09",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p7",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p7",
      "textEn": "I felt two things at once: relieved, and a little ashamed that I had never really learned her name, even after living here a year. I went down the hall and knocked.",
      "spans": [],
      "parentId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p8",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p8",
      "textEn": "Mrs. Tan opened the door with a smile, as if this were a normal Tuesday. The box was on a chair behind her, still sealed. \"It's heavier than it looks,\" she said. \"I didn't want someone to walk into it.\"",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 20,
          "end": 24,
          "surface": "door",
          "cardId": "l13-w-door",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p9",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p9",
      "textEn": "I thanked her more than once. She waved it off and asked if the lamp was for me. I told her it was for my sister, and that I had been worried it would not come in time.",
      "spans": [],
      "parentId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p10",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p10",
      "textEn": "That evening, I went back with a small bag of fruit from the market. She said I didn't need to do that, but she took two peaches, and we talked for a few minutes about the plants in her hallway window.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 186,
          "end": 193,
          "surface": "hallway",
          "cardId": "reading-delivery-w09",
          "form": "exact",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box"
    },
    {
      "id": "everyday-reading-pack-v5::reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p11",
      "sourcePack": "everyday-reading-pack-v5",
      "sourceVersion": "v5",
      "unitType": "reading-paragraph",
      "sourceId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box-p11",
      "textEn": "The lamp was fine, and I packed it carefully for Friday. What stayed with me was simpler: I live next to people, not just next to doors. The next time I pass 4A, I will say hello by name.",
      "spans": [
        {
          "start": 130,
          "end": 135,
          "surface": "doors",
          "cardId": "l13-w-door",
          "form": "variant",
          "priority": "primary"
        }
      ],
      "parentId": "reading-neighbor-kept-the-box"
    }
  ],
  "stats": {
